. After being told that his end was approaching by his longtime friend and physician, Kinzo is desperate to meet his life's true love one last time: the Golden Witch, Beatrice. Having immersed himself in black magic for many of the later years in his life, Kinzo instigates a ceremony to revive his beloved upon his family's arrival on Rokkenjima. Soon after, a violent typhoon traps the family on the island and a string of mysterious murders commence, forcing the eighteen people on the island to fight for their lives in a deadly struggle between fantasy and reality.\n\n(Source: MAL Rewrite, edited)"},"tags":[{"name":"Tragedy","rank":96,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Achronological Order","rank":91,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Witch","rank":89,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Death Game","rank":88,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Magic","rank":87,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Detective","rank":85,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ojou-sama","rank":85,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Butler","rank":85,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Alternate Universe","rank":81,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Gore","rank":78,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Adult Cast","rank":77,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Meta","rank":77,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Ensemble Cast","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Maids","rank":74,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":67,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dissociative Identities","rank":66,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Guns","rank":62,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Crossover","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"LGBTQ+ Themes","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Transgender","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Bar","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Demons","rank":56,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Curses","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kuudere","rank":42,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Time Skip","rank":38,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Tsundere","rank":20,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Kemonomimi","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Denpa","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Umineko: When They Cry","english":"Umineko: Wh